<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n88954" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">προσεδρ-εύω</span></b> , <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>sit near, wait</i> or <i>watch beside</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πυρᾷ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>Or.</u>
					403
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">π. τινί</span>
			<i>to be always at</i> his <i>side, keep watch on</i> him, <i><span class="en">
				D.
				34.26
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τοῖς πράγμασι, τοῖς
			καιροῖς</span>, <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				1.18
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Plb.
				38.13.9
			</span></i>; [<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τοῖς ἐφήβοις] προσκαρτερῶν
				ἐπιμελῶς καὶ -εύων</span>, of a <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κοσμητής</span>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>IG</u>
				22.1028.84
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">π. τῷ θεῷ</span>
			<i>wait upon</i> God, <i><span class="en">
				J.
				<u>AJ</u>
				3.4.1
			</span></i>; <i>attend to</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τοῖς τῆς Ἀσίας πράγμασιν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>AJA</u>
					18.327
				</span></i>
			 (Sardis, <span class="entity">i B.C.</span>), cf. <i><span class="en">
				<u>CIG</u>
				2715.18
			</span></i> (<span class="entity">Stratonicea</span>); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τῇ θεραπείᾳ τοῦ θεοῦ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					J.
					<u>Ap.</u>
					1.7
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τοῖς ὑπομνήμασι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plb.
					12.26d
				</span></i>
			.<i><span class="en">
				5
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Phld.
				<u>Rh.</u>
				2.61
			</span></i>
			<i><span class="en">
				S.
			</span></i>, al.: abs., <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>HA</u>
				568b15
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Plb.
				11.4.2
			</span></i>; <i>watch</i> the rise of the Nile, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Sammelb.</u>
				6597
			</span></i>
			<span class="entity">(iii A.D.)</span>, al.; <i>persist in</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ταῖς φιλοπονίαις</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Arist.
					<u>Pol.</u>
					1338b25
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τῷ πόθῳ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Alex.
					234
				</span></i>
			; <i>apply oneself</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λίαν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Arist.
					<u>Pol.</u>
					1337b16
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πρὸς ἴδιον</span> to one's own
			affairs, ib. <i><span class="en">
				1263a29
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εἰς τὰ μαθήματα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>PSI</u>
					1.94.8
				</span></i>
			
			<span class="entity">(ii A.D.)</span>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>besiege</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ταῖς Συρακούσαις</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plb.
					8.7.11
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b>
			<i>wait</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">προσέδρευσα ἐφ᾽ ἡμέρας δύο
					ἐκδεχόμενός σε</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>BGU</u>
					892.5
				</span></i>
			
			<span class="entity">(ii A.D.)</span>; esp. <i>attend</i> at a law-court, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">παρεῖναι καὶ π. τῷ βήματι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>PAmh.</u>
					2.81.9
				</span></i>
			
			<span class="entity">(iii A.D.)</span>; <i>attend regularly, serve</i>, as clerk
			of the court, ib.<i><span class="en">
				82.3
			</span></i>
			<span class="entity">(iii/iv A.D.)</span>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>POxy.</u>
				59.10
			</span></i>
			<span class="entity">(iii A.D.)</span>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>4.</b>
			<i>to be in seruice, serve</i>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πρὸς τῷ
				διδασκαλείῳ</span> (as a menial), <i><span class="en">
				D.
				18.258
			</span></i>; of an apprentice, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">π. τῷ διδασκάλῳ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>POxy.</u>
					725.10
				</span></i>
			
			<span class="entity">(ii A.D.)</span>; of a servant, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">παραμένειν . . καὶ π</span>. <i><span class="en">
				<u>PStrassb.</u>
				40.31
			</span></i>
			<span class="entity">(vi A.D.)</span>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
